# Zod 4 string formats

This project uses **Zod 4** (`zod` ^4). Prefer top-level format helpers over methods on `z.string()` that TypeScript marks as **deprecated**.

## UUID

```ts
// ❌ BAD — deprecated on ZodString
z.string().uuid()

// ✅ GOOD
z.uuid()
```

Same idea for other formats when available on the package top level, e.g. `z.email()`, `z.url()`, `z.iso.datetime()` — use the Zod 4 API, not the old chained validators, if the IDE flags them as deprecated.

## Do

- Match existing call sites that already use `z.uuid()` (e.g. dedication accept routes).
- Keep `.uuid()` only if you deliberately need a chained `ZodString` API and have confirmed it is not deprecated in the installed Zod version.

## Avoid

- Reintroducing `z.string().uuid()` (or other deprecated `ZodString` format methods) in new schemas.
